{"text":"{
  "status": "NEEDS_IMPROVEMENT",
  "core_findings": [
    "Electronics has the weakest positive–negative separation: 14.95% of negatives outrank positives, and its 10th-percentile margin is -0.4812. Movies_and_TV separates sampled pairs most strongly, with a mean margin of 7.7963 and only 3.03% wrong rankings.",
    "Industrial_and_Scientific and CDs_and_Vinyl show intermediate separation, with wrong-ranking rates of 8.22% and 9.14%. Embedding similarity scores cluster near 0.5 (0.5392–0.5566), providing little evidence of severe directional collapse."
  ],
  "key_implications": [
    "Pairwise ranking reliability varies substantially across datasets, with Electronics showing the most confusion.",
    "Positive mean margins coexist with weak or incorrect rankings in the lower tail; these diagnostics alone do not establish validation HR@10 or training convergence."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "headline_metrics": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": 0.1495,
      "Electronics:pos_neg_margin_p10": -0.4812,
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": 0.2115,
      "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": 0.0303
    },
    "brief_metric_read": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": "21.15% of measured margins fall below 0.5, including negative margins.",
      "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": "Only 3.03% of sampled negatives score above their positives."
    }
  }
}"}
